Our implementation will:
1. Parse incoming packets.
2. Filter out packets that match a block signature (specifically, any UDP packet sent to port `9999` starting with the payload `"DROP"`).
3. If not dropped, **forward** the packet back out of the same network interface with swapped MAC addresses (a high-speed reflector/forwarder), bypassing the rest of the OS network stack entirely.

