2. **Infinite Impulse Response (IIR) Filtering:**
   To filter noise, a Moving Average Filter usually requires storing an array of the last $N$ samples (which eats up precious RAM). The **EMA filter** used here acts as a Low-Pass filter but only requires storing *one* previous state (`stored_value`), saving 99% of the memory.
