To demonstrate a practical, high-performance implementation, we will build a **Native C++ Physics Plugin** designed to integrate with **Unity** (though this C-compatible interface can also be used in Unreal Engine or Godot). 

This plugin implements a lightweight 3D particle/sphere physics solver with gravity, Euler integration, and ground-plane collision resolution with elastic bouncing (restitution).

